# Template for e2e/.env — copy it, then adjust the URL if your app is elsewhere:
#
#     cp e2e/.env.example e2e/.env
#
# The real .env is git-ignored so each machine can point at its own app.
#
# Shared configuration for every e2e test under e2e/ (Playwright specs in tests/
# and the shell smoke tests in smoke/). Both readers parse this same file, so the
# app URL is defined in exactly one place.
#
# E2E_BASE_URL is the SPA entry point of the app under test. Everything else is
# derived from it:
#   origin    -> http://localhost:9380        (Playwright baseURL; specs goto '/app/...')
#   app base  -> http://localhost:9380/app    (smoke scripts: login.php, service.php)
E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9380/app/ui/

# ── Marketplace / licence SystemData ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Injected into the TESTING database by e2e/bootstrap/seed-systemdata.sh before any
# e2e or integration run. Without them every extensions-pro module (leave,
# performance, training, loans, recruitment, learn, expenses) renders
# "No active IceHrmPro license" instead of its content, and ~40 specs fail as
# "element not visible".
#
# Values are base64 of the raw SystemData.value (PHP-serialised) so each fits on one
# line. They are REAL credentials from a licensed instance — e2e/.env is git-ignored,
# so they stay on your machine. Never paste them into a tracked file.
#
# Populate from a licensed environment (defaults to the dev stack):
#   e2e/bootstrap/seed-systemdata.sh --export >> e2e/.env
E2E_SYSTEMDATA_MARKETPLACE_CONNECTION_B64=
E2E_SYSTEMDATA_MARKETPLACE_MY_EXTENSIONS_B64=
